<title>EGYPT: Egypt impounds Panama ship for unpaid fuel bill.</title>
<headline>Egypt impounds Panama ship for unpaid fuel bill.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-01-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian authorities have impounded at Port Suez a Panamanian cargo ship because it did not pay a $35,000 fuel bill, port sources said on Saturday.</p>
<p>They said the Oriental Iris, en route to the Iranian port Bandar Khomeini from Tunisia, was impounded while it was sailing through the Suez Canal.</p>
<p>The sources said the ship, which was carrying 8,296 tonnes of phosphoric acid, had not paid for fuel it had taken on board on a previous trip.</p>
</text>
